<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR mostly lower on high liquidity.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR mostly lower on high liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly lower due to the excess liquidity in the system, traders said.</p>
<p>The one-week to one-month and the one-year rates were all weaker, while the two and three-month PHIBOR were unchanged.</p>
<p>&quot;The PHIBOR market is soft mainly because of the excess liquidity flooding the system,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Only the six-month PHIBOR inched up marginally, but traders viewed it as an aberration.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 MAY 28		  MAY 26</p>
<p>    1 W		14  5/8		 14 3/4</p>
<p>    2 W		12 13/16		13</p>
<p>    1 M		11  5/8		 11 11/16</p>
<p>    2 M		11  1/2		 11 1/2</p>
<p>    3 M		11  3/8		 11 3/8</p>
<p>    6 M		11  3/16		11 1/8</p>
<p>    12M		11  1/8		 11 3/16</p>
<p>    VAL		29-May		  28-May</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
